course: dictionary
lesson: 15505
title: Subdued
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Subdued means quiet and a little sad or tired, not lively as usual. The words around it are the clues. «Ben hardly smiled all day and sat very still. He seemed subdued.» Ben is not shouting or laughing, so subdued must mean quiet and low.
explain: Subdued can also describe light, colours and sounds. Subdued light is soft and gentle, not bright. Subdued colours are muted, not bright. A subdued voice is quiet, not loud. Ask yourself: is this about a feeling, or about a light, colour or sound?
explain: Subdued can be a verb too. «The rebels were subdued» means they were brought under control, usually by a stronger group. Check the sentence: if it describes how someone feels or looks, it means quiet or sad. If someone was forced under control, it is the verb.
fact: Subdued means quiet and a little sad or tired, not lively as usual.
fact: «A subdued mood» means people feel quiet and not very cheerful.
fact: «Subdued lighting» is soft and gentle, not bright.
fact: «In a subdued voice» means speaking quietly.
fact: As a verb, «subdued» means brought under control, as in «The rebels were subdued».
exercise: «Ben hardly smiled all day. He seemed subdued.» What does subdued mean here? | Covered in mud | *Quiet and a little sad or tired | Loud and very excited | Brightly coloured
exercise: «The café had subdued lighting, so the room felt calm and cosy.» What does subdued lighting mean? | *Soft and gentle, not bright | Flashing on and off | Very bright and harsh | Coming from a torch shining at a wall
exercise: «He spoke in a subdued voice so the baby would not wake.» What does subdued mean in this sentence? | Loud and proud | *Quiet and soft | Happy and bouncy | Angry and fast
test: «The rebels were subdued by the army.» In this sentence, subdued means: | *Brought under control | Gave up their homes | Made very happy | Painted in soft colours
test: Which phrase means soft and muted colours? | Stripy colours | *Subdued colours | Bright colours | Loud colours
exam: Jess says, «The room felt subdued after the news.» What does subdued suggest about the mood? | Extra bright and cheerful | *Quiet and a little sad | A wild party | Very angry shouting
